# Reproducibility freeze — "Which substrate computes?" method note

Frozen environment for the method note in `paper/` (compiled PDF: `paper/main.pdf`).

## Environment
- Python 3.12 venv: `02_cl\.venv312\` (numpy 2.5.3, matplotlib 3.11.2).
  - On this machine the interpreter is at:
    `C:\Proyectos\papers\Icra2027\02_cl\.venv312\Scripts\python.exe`
  - A normal venv with numpy+matplotlib is sufficient.
- MiKTeX (light compiler, user-installed; on PATH). `latexmk -pdf` or
  `pdflatex` twice from `paper/` rebuilds `main.pdf`.

## Reproduce the artifact pipeline
From the repo root (`sandbox/`):

1. Regenerate tables + figures from the stored JSON summaries
   (no hand-typed numbers, no reruns needed):
   ```
   python build_figures_tables.py
   ```
   Writes `paper/tables/{tab_gateb,tab_gated,tab_gatee,canonical_numbers}.tex`
   and `paper/figures/{decoder_bars.png,...}` (canonical.png is copied from
   `../surrogate_cl/results/task_tracking.png`; see `paper/figures/ATTRIBUTION.txt`).
2. Rebuild the video (needs matplotlib + a runnable ffmpeg):
   ```
   python make_video.py
   ```
   Writes `video/pulse_raster.mp4`.
3. Recompile the note:
   ```
   cd paper
   pdflatex main.tex   (twice; or latexmk -pdf main.tex)
   ```

## Full empirical runs (the experiments themselves)
- Gate B (substrate swap, fixed readout): `gate_b/run.py`
- Gate D (readout check, same spikes): `gate_d/run.py`
- Gate E (memory tasks): `gate_e/run.py`
Each writes a JSON summary under its `results/`; summaries are committed so the
note is reproducible from the artifacts alone.
- Robustness checks live in `verify/` (ridge-vs-direct, dead-null exactness,
  readout-channel ablation); see `paper/` §Verification.

## Canonical numbers note
The close-loop canonical battery numbers cited in the note
(RMSE 0.238; p_1s=0.0156; p_2s=0.0312; d_z=-8.58/-2.43/-38.94) are owned by the
tracking session (`surrogate_cl/results/task_tracking.json`) and are read-only
here; only copied into `paper/figures/` with attribution.

